{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed</b> Three times in the Masorah: this one, and <b>ויסע מצאן עמו</b> (and he journeyed from the sheep with him) — teaches that they were finding precious stones in the bed of the sea, and Moses moved them against their will like this sheep that a shepherd moves from flock to flock. And another one in Job: <b>ויסע כעץ תקותי</b> (and he uprooted like a tree my hope) — through Pharaoh who was with him in his counsel in harsh labor, he was repaid measure for measure, as stated: <b>ויסע כעץ תקותי</b>."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:06.114667825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}